  "order": 48,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "j1z4b9e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Budget"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Under Article 112 of the Indian Constitution, the Union Budget is officially termed the Annual Financial Statement.",
        "The Financial Year in India begins on April 1 and ends on March 31 of the following year.",
        "Budgetary receipts are categorized into Revenue Receipts (non-liability creating) and Capital Receipts (liability creating or asset reducing).",
        "Goods and Services Tax (GST) represents a major indirect tax reform implemented across India on July 1, 2017.",
        "A Budget Deficit occurs when government total expenditure exceeds total receipts in a financial year."
      ],
      "id": "xs2e5rv"
    },
